  "result": "Excellent! All 173 tests pass. I've successfully added credit note support:\n\n**New error code in `src/errors.js`:**\n- `CREDIT_TOO_HIGH` \u2014 Credit note amount exceeds the invoice total\n\n**New file `src/credits.js` with `createCreditNote()` function:**\n\n**`createCreditNote(invoice, { amount, reason, date }, existingNumbers)`** \u2014 Creates a credit note for refunds:\n- Returns `ok(creditNote)` with:\n  - `number` \u2014 CN-<year>-<counter> format (separate counter from invoices)\n  - `invoiceNumber` \u2014 the invoice being credited\n  - `customerId` \u2014 the customer\n  - `amount` \u2014 refund amount in cents\n  - `reason` \u2014 refund reason\n  - `date` \u2014 credit note issue date\n- Validates:\n  - Invoice status is 'issued', 'partially_paid', or 'paid' (NOT_ISSUED for draft)\n  - Amount is a positive integer (AMOUNT_INVALID)\n  - Amount doesn't exceed invoice total (CREDIT_TOO_HIGH)\n- Credit notes numbered independently from invoices:\n  - Format: CN-<year>-<counter>\n  - Counter is 4 digits, zero-padded, starting at 0001 per year\n  - Separate counter from invoices (e.g., can have INV-2024-0001 and CN-2024-0001)\n  - Restarts at 0001 each calendar year\n\n**Tests (11 credit note tests added):**\n- Creating credit notes for issued, partially paid, and paid invoices\n- Rejecting draft invoices\n- Amount validation (integer, positive, no negatives)\n- Rejecting amounts exceeding invoice total\n- Counter incrementing within a year\n- Counter restarting for new year\n- Handling mixed invoice and credit note numbers in existingNumbers\n\nThe credit note system integrates seamlessly with invoices and enables proper refund tracking with independent numbering.",
